<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>出版物 |皮尤研究中心</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/publications/</link><description>塑造您世界的数字、事实和趋势</description><lastBuildDate>Sat, 01 Aug 2026 05:25:56 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>国际社会对美国及其总统的看法越来越相关</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/decoded/2026/08/28/international-views-of-the-us-and-its-president-are-increasingly-correlated/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/08/d_26.08.28_pres_us_correlated_crop.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;在乔·拜登担任总统期间以及特朗普的第一个任期内，对美国的看法与对总统的信心之间的关系要弱得多。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 02:09:09 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/decoded/2026/08/28/international-views-of-the-us-and-its-president-are-increasingly-correlated/</guid></item><item><title>超过一半的 40 多岁美国人夹在年迈的父母和自己的孩子之间</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/27/more-than-half-of-americans-in-their-40s-are-sandwiched-between-an-aging-parent-and-their-own-children/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2022/04/FT_22.04.01_SandwichGeneration_feature.jpg?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;总体而言，25% 的美国成年人的父母年龄在 65 岁或以上，并且有一个 18 岁以下的孩子、一个接受经济支持的成年孩子或两者兼而有之。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 21:23:39 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/27/more-than-half-of-americans-in-their-40s-are-sandwiched-between-an-aging-parent-and-their-own-children/</guid></item><item><title>在线选择参与民意调查中的虚假受访者不容易修复</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/methods/2026/08/27/no-easy-fix-for-bogus-respondents-in-online-opt-in-polls/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/08/PM_2026.08.26_bogus-respondents_crop@2x.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;一项检查在线选择加入民意调查的新研究发现，虽然删除虚假受访者通常可以提高数据质量，但没有一种方法可以可靠地解决这个问题。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 21:23:39 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/methods/2026/08/27/no-easy-fix-for-bogus-respondents-in-online-opt-in-polls/</guid></item><item><title>37个国家的许多人对联合国持积极态度，但有些地方的看法变得更加消极</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/27/many-across-37-countries-view-the-un-favorably-but-opinions-have-become-more-negative-in-some-places/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/08/SR_26.08.27_views-of-un_featured.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt; 37 个国家中，有 55% 的人对联合国持正面看法，尽管近年来一些国家的看法变得更加负面。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 21:23:39 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/27/many-across-37-countries-view-the-un-favorably-but-opinions-have-become-more-negative-in-some-places/</guid></item><item><title>与十年前相比，如今使用现金的美国人有所减少，但许多人仍然携带现金</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/26/fewer-americans-use-cash-today-than-a-decade-ago-but-many-still-carry-it/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/08/PI_26.08.20_Cashless_featured.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;如今，42% 的美国成年人表示，他们通常一周不会使用现金进行任何购物。这比 2015 年的 24% 有所上升。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 21:23:39 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/26/fewer-americans-use-cash-today-than-a-decade-ago-but-many-still-carry-it/</guid></item></channel></rss>